[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3834254520","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115653#issuecomment-3834254520","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115653","id":3834254520,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kihS4","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-02T10:25:23Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T10:25:23Z","body":"Just a nitpick on the commit/PR title, it's not clear what \"Atlas_Update_Texture\" refers to. Identifiers with underscores should be reserved for actual references to code (with backticks), but there's no \"Atlas_Update_Texture\" code in this PR (there's `texture_atlas_update_texture` in GLES3 and it's named differently in RD.\r\n\r\nSo it would be better to use plain English than proto-code for this. See https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#format-your-commit-messages-with-readability-in-mind for details on how we prefer commit messages to be written.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3834254520/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3883547952","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115653#issuecomment-3883547952","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115653","id":3883547952,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nej0w","user":{"login":"coobenguy","id":76452238,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDUyMjM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76452238?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy","html_url":"https://github.com/coobenguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-11T10:28:23Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T10:28:23Z","body":"This would also allow for animated light projectors right?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3883547952/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3931032196","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115653#issuecomment-3931032196","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115653","id":3931032196,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qTsqE","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-20T01:15:47Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T01:15:57Z","body":"> This would also allow for animated light projectors right?\r\n\r\nProjectors use their own atlas, but it works in the same way as decals. I didn't test if projectors work with animated DrawableTextures now, but it should be easy to implement if it doesn't work already with the PR.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3931032196/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3931730067","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115653#issuecomment-3931730067","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115653","id":3931730067,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qWXCT","user":{"login":"ColinSORourke","id":44822820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODIyODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44822820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinSORourke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-20T05:17:42Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T05:17:42Z","body":"@Calinou @coobenguy I just tested this, and it seems like the case!\r\n\r\nI set up a Spotlight3D, and had a GDScript initialize the Light_Projector texture to a new DrawableTexture, and then a timer callback to blit the Light_Projector between two possible textures. It correctly 'animated' the light projector","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3931730067/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4177587922","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115653#issuecomment-4177587922","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115653","id":4177587922,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75AO7S","user":{"login":"mertkasar","id":2726562,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjY1NjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2726562?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mertkasar","html_url":"https://github.com/mertkasar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mertkasar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mertkasar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mertkasar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mertkasar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mertkasar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mertkasar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mertkasar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mertkasar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mertkasar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-02T12:40:02Z","updated_at":"2026-04-02T12:40:02Z","body":"A little test on DrawableTexture as projector... literally... 👀\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/715afc9d-94e5-4377-94e9-3067ccb3d1af\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4177587922/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":7,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4178157995","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115653#issuecomment-4178157995","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115653","id":4178157995,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75CaGr","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-02T14:09:15Z","updated_at":"2026-04-19T21:26:00Z","body":"I wonder if this could be called in ViewportTexture when it's redrawn. While we want to encourage DrawableTexture when possible as it's less demanding, some use cases are better served by ViewportTexture.\r\n\r\nIf the Viewport has its update mode set correctly, it should only redraw when needed (or only redraw once), so there shouldn't be a significant performance cost otherwise. It should suppress the need for more demanding `get_texture()` workarounds, which should overall be a performance win. Implementing this would effectively close https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/73400.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4178157995/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4276477693","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115653#issuecomment-4276477693","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115653","id":4276477693,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7-5d79","user":{"login":"TheMagnat","id":45939503,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1OTM5NTAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45939503?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMagnat","html_url":"https://github.com/TheMagnat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMagnat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMagnat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMagnat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMagnat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMagnat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMagnat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMagnat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMagnat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheMagnat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-19T17:53:11Z","updated_at":"2026-04-19T17:53:11Z","body":"> I wonder if this could be called in ViewportTexture when it's redrawn. While we want to encourage DrawableTexture when possible as it's less demanding, some use cases are better served by ViewportTexture.\r\n> \r\n> If the Viewport has its update mode set correctly, it should only redraw when needed (or only redraw once), so there shouldn't be a significant performance cost otherwise. It should suppress the need for more demanding `get_texture()` workarounds, which should overall be a performance win.\r\n\r\nI've created a PR on the branch from this PR to add this feature : https://github.com/ColinSORourke/godot/pull/1\r\nBut I'm not certain on my implementation, this feature require managing proxy texture, update the used variable so that the Viewport get updated on visible update mode. Maybe we should valid this feature directly and add the viewport feature on another PR ?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4276477693/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5433343453","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115653#issuecomment-5433343453","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115653","id":5433343453,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQ9o93Q","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T01:50:54Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T01:50:54Z","body":"Discussed this in render meeting. There might be an optimised way to handle updating the decals in the RD renderer and updating the mipmaps in one go, but that would involve a compute shader that only can be trusted upon in the Forward+ renderer.\r\n\r\nFor a first implementation the more generic current approach is likely more than good enough.\r\n\r\nGenerally agree with the approach taken so gets a thumbs up from me.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5433343453/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":4,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5701064434","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115653#issuecomment-5701064434","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115653","id":5701064434,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABU89W8g","user":{"login":"QbieShay","id":7917475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MTc0NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7917475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay","html_url":"https://github.com/QbieShay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-16T16:39:51Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T16:39:51Z","body":"Tested a bit the PR. My test is done by using projectors and decals.\r\n\r\n2 things i noticed, not really related to this PR but more to drawable texture:\r\n\r\n1. setting mip to -1 crashes the engine with a segmentation fault\r\n2. attempting to blit to a texture that was instantiated in editor causes mipmap errors, but the real error is that no setup() was called on the texture. The error message isn't really helpful because it points to mipmap.\r\n\r\nHere's my little diorama:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5d3ebbd3-2618-4322-a748-1e15900a2b06\r\n\r\nI didn't understand how I'd go about doing a blit directly on the decal atlas if i wanted to do it from the rendering server, there's no documentation on this PR, so as far as I can tell, the only way to use this is to use it via the nodes? How would I go about using this without the nodes?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5701064434/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5702668746","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115653#issuecomment-5702668746","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115653","id":5702668746,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABU-fRyg","user":{"login":"ColinSORourke","id":44822820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODIyODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44822820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinSORourke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-16T18:38:59Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T18:38:59Z","body":"@QbieShay Thanks for the feedback! I'll get right on addressing those DrawableTexture issues.\r\n\r\n> I didn't understand how I'd go about doing a blit directly on the decal atlas if i wanted to do it from the rendering server, there's no documentation on this PR, so as far as I can tell, the only way to use this is to use it via the nodes? How would I go about using this without the nodes?\r\n\r\nThis PR wasn't intended to add a user-exposed API, but an internal API for DrawableTextures, and other textures that may be modified. When those textures are changed, they can use the internal API to mark themselves as 'draw_dirty', indicating that the Atlas should be updated, but does not require a full rebuild.\r\n\r\nI'm unsure if we should or how we would want to expose this to users. I'd be happy to work on an implementation if that is desired though!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5702668746/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5703704985","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115653#issuecomment-5703704985","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115653","id":5703704985,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABU_ehmQ","user":{"login":"QbieShay","id":7917475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MTc0NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7917475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay","html_url":"https://github.com/QbieShay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github